I continue walking across the flea market.
A table with old electronics looks very interesting.
I stop and look at the things.
Between old radios I discover two beautiful cameras.
I ask the vendor about the prices.
"Excuse me, what does this camera cost?" I ask and point to one model.
"Hello," the man says warmly.
"That one costs sixty euros, it still works great."
"And what does that camera cost?" I ask and point to the other model.
"That one is a bit cheaper, only forty euros."
"Do you like taking photos?" he then asks me.
"Yes, very much," I answer him.
"But today I mostly shoot digitally."
"I bought my digital camera many years ago."
We chat briefly about old technology.
I do not buy anything and leave the cameras lying on the table.
I enjoy the nice conversation today more than the shopping.
I say goodbye and slowly walk on.
